From: Prithwiraj Samanta <prskid1000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 08:29:38 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] telecode: shader fill inputs - GLSL, time, mouse, backdrop,
 SDF, export rasteriser

Shader fills take GLSL as well as SkSL: a Shadertoy-style mainImage or a
void main() writing gl_FragColor is translated (entry point, y-up
coordinates, iResolution/iTime/iMouse/iChannel0, sampler2D, #define and
#ifdef GL_ES), and what cannot be translated (discard, derivatives, #if,
gl_FragCoord outside main, other channels) is refused with its line;
compiler errors are mapped back to the author's lines. Uniform
annotations (@color @label @min @max @step @range @default) describe
controls; @time and @mouse (or iTime/iMouse, u_time/u_mouse) take the frame
time and the pointer in node pixels; @backdrop (or backdrop/iChannel0)
is a child shader of what is painted behind the layer; sdf(p) is the
signed distance to the layer outline (exact EDT of the rasterised shape).
Presets gain annotations and plasma (GLSL, animated), frosted (backdrop)
and outline_glow (sdf). SkSL -> GLSL ES 1.0 and GLSL-for-WebGL for exports.
The SVG/PDF writer asks a registered rasteriser for procedural fills
(else paints the fallback), and the .fig writer stores a procedural paint
as SOLID keeping customEffectId, so other readers see the fallback while
the definition round-trips.
